  "live_records": {
    "q-114071": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114071",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/5fe08f28818914a3cc95e880d7d83bef11ed58d6cba7265331bb0baeac341935.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find $m∠QOS.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/6d958d3fe726049f7f737ea8d43f9659734154c79fcc19e3eba3090f68aef295.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠QOR$ and $∠ROS$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OR}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QOS & =m∠QOR+m∠ROS \\\\  & ={68}^{∘}+{54}^{∘} \\\\  & ={122}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
