    "q-150761": {
      "dom_id": "step-q150761",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/39e491930076760f06a77929e4264d41ba3f921db918fb34dd49772036ad09d5.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find $m∠QOS.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/537b98b49691a55102fd5c1d06f6635f770118113b3535e8c1238f169b2e4dfb.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠QOR$ and $∠ROS$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OR}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QOS & =m∠QOR+m∠ROS \\\\  & ={79}^{∘}+{41}^{∘} \\\\  & ={120}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
