    "q-154676": {
      "dom_id": "step-q154676",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/775743da6dbc3f706f70b1d8a71b62ee4453147519ac7d242c9ba242165efe6e.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find $m∠AOC.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/edd8c0ca83fc53b81b69d21ebc73c43287777f4bb9252b099078750a194981e8.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠AOB$ and $∠BOC$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OB}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC & =m∠AOB+m∠BOC \\\\  & ={36}^{∘}+{48}^{∘} \\\\  & ={84}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
