    "q-150762": {
      "dom_id": "step-q150762",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/46db75fc773bb1fbcb21817fe8371b855c8f9ac8a08e88134fa992dd68498982.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $m∠BAD={80}^{∘}.$ What equation could be used to find the value of $x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠BAC.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAC$ and $∠CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠BAC$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠CAD).$\n\nTherefore, the correct equation to determine $x$ is the following:\n\n$$\nx={80}^{∘}-{60}^{∘}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-150762-a",
