    "q-150766": {
      "dom_id": "step-q150766",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/c4c1194c822c34e02e73e130c2c39e99a98cb52b577c9d68be4c29554604fc0f.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $m∠LON={90}^{∘}.$ What equation could be used to find the value of $x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠LOM.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠LOM$ and $∠MON$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{OM}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠LON)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠LOM$ and $∠MON).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠LOM$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠LON)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠MON).$\n\nTherefore, the correct equation to determine $x$ is the following:\n\n$$\nx={90}^{∘}-{25}^{∘}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-150766-a",
