      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/12f9e7857f065a6fc457533c25adc4a00cdf4c325838a5865abd87d6fba90c4a.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠BAE={160}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠DAE.$\n\nThe measure of $∠DAE$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAE)$ and the two smaller known angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx={160}^{∘}-{72}^{∘}-{63}^{∘}={25}^{∘}.\n$$",
